                        ],
                        "kind": "monospace",
                        "roles": []
                      },
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": " can be used in integration tests which start an external server on an available random port. However, these utilities make no guarantee about the subsequent availability of a given port and are therefore unreliable. Instead of using "
                      },
                      {
                        "id": null,
                        "inlines": [
                          {
                            "kind": "text",
                            "value": "TestSocketUtils"
                          }
                        ],
                        "kind": "monospace",
                        "roles": []
                      },
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": " to find an available local port for a server, it is recommended that you rely on a server’s ability to start on a random ephemeral port that it selects or is assigned by the operating system. To interact with that server, you should query the server for the port it is currently using."
                      }
